{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01E8NJdKMtU21RpCauCo65Cs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and propose tasks for release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum).\n\nLooking at the constraints:\n- Max 1 task\n- 150-250 lines production code\n- Max 4 PRD sub-requirements per task\n- Release scope: only 05.4\n\nI need to find the PRD for the checksum utilities. The project context mentions prd for these but doesn't include the actual PRD content. Let me work with what I have.\n\nThe use cases are:\n- rel05.4-uc001-md5sum\n\n\n- rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum\n- rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum\n- rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum\n\nAll have specstatus: spec_complete, codestatus: not started. Since I can only propose 1 task and these four utilities are nearly identical in structure—they all read files or stdin, compute a hash, and output in the standard format—I should consolidate them into a single implementation task that covers all four algorithms. I need to figure out which PRD to reference since the checksum utilities aren't explicitly listed in the context. Looking at the pattern of existing PRDs and the use case numbering, I should construct the task by referencing the most likely PRD path, though I'll need to make an educated guess about whether these are covered under a single PRD or multiple ones.\n\nSince I can only propose one task and these four utilities are nearly identical in structure, I'll bundle the implementation of all four checksum commands together—each needs flag parsing and hash computation logic, totaling around 160-240 lines which fits the budget. I'll anchor this to the specific requirement IDs from the PRD once I determine the correct file reference.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27516,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27516},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c54928-3f93-4b15-98eb-98ccf3f4621f","uuid":"c4b6953e-3663-4daf-82ca-4b2185a66e9a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01E8NJdKMtU21RpCauCo65Cs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates Unix utilities in Go, verified via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Specs live in docs/, implementations in cmd/ and pkg/, differential testing harness in pkg/testutils/. Magefiles drive the orchestrator.\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 05.3 are spec_complete/implemented. Release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) has specs written but no code generated. All four use cases are at `spec_complete` / `codestatus: not started`.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.4 — four checksum utilities sharing nearly identical structure (read input, compute hash, output `hash  filename` format, support `--check` mode).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 05.4 is the earliest incomplete release. All four checksum utilities (md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) follow the same pattern with only the hash algorithm differing. Each utility is ~40-60 lines of production code, so all four fit within the 150-250 line budget as a single implementation task.\n\nNo new pkg/ dependencies are needed — Go's `crypto/md5`, `crypto/sha1`, `crypto/sha256`, `crypto/sha512` packages provide all hash algorithms. These utilities depend on pkg/sys (SIGPIPE handler) and pkg/testutils (differential tests) which already exist.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement checksum quartet cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum (rel05.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the PRD covering md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum -- read all requirements)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml (use case for md5sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml (use case for sha1sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml (use case for sha256sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml (use case for sha512sum)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml (test suite for all four utilities)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols: differential testing, SIGPIPE handling, graceful skip)\n      - docs/engineering/ (read all engineering guidelines for coding conventions)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler -- call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() in each main)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (read all files to understand DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference for flag parsing, stdin/file handling, and main structure)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference for differential test structure)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (reference for multi-file processing pattern)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (reference for differential test with multiple inputs)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: md5sum implementation using crypto/md5\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gmd5sum\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha1sum implementation using crypto/sha1\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha1sum\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha256sum implementation using crypto/sha256\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha256sum\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum implementation using crypto/sha512\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha512sum\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum as four\n          separate cmd/ packages. Each reads from files listed on the command line\n          or from stdin when no files are given (or when \"-\" is specified). Each\n          computes the corresponding hash and prints output in GNU coreutils format:\n          \"<hex-hash>  <filename>\\n\" (two spaces before filename, \"-\" for stdin).\n          Use crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256, crypto/sha512 from the Go\n          standard library. Read all PRD requirements for these utilities and\n          implement every flag and behavior specified.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement --check (-c) mode for all four utilities. In check mode, read\n          lines from the checksum file in the format \"<hash>  <filename>\" or\n          \"<hash> <filename>\" (binary or text mode marker). For each line, compute\n          the hash of the named file and compare. Print \"<filename>: OK\" or\n          \"<filename>: FAILED\". After all lines, if any failed, print a summary\n          line to stderr: \"WARNING: N computed checksum(s) did NOT match\" and exit 1.\n          Support --warn (-w), --quiet, and --strict flags as specified in the PRD.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement --binary (-b) and --text (-t) flag handling. On Unix these do\n          not change behavior (files are always read in binary mode) but affect the\n          mode indicator in output: \"*\" prefix for binary mode, \" \" (space) for text\n          mode. Default is text mode on Unix. In --check mode, accept both markers.\n          Support --tag flag to output BSD-style checksums if specified in the PRD.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement differential tests for all four utilities. Each test file follows\n          the project's shared differential testing protocol: build the Go binary with\n          testutils.BuildBinary, find the GNU reference binary via exec.LookPath\n          (gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, gsha512sum), skip gracefully if the\n          reference binary is not found, define []testutils.DiffTest cases covering\n          stdin, single file, multiple files, --check mode, --binary, --text, missing\n          files (exit code 1), and empty input. Run testutils.RunDiffTests to compare.\n          Cover at least the test cases specified in test-rel-05.4.yaml.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          All four utilities share the same command structure. Study the PRD and\n          existing cmd/ implementations (especially cmd/cat and cmd/wc) to match\n          the project's established patterns for flag parsing (use the flag package),\n          stdin/file iteration, error handling, and exit codes. Call\n          sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of each main().\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Do NOT create a shared internal package for checksum logic. Each cmd/\n          package is self-contained with its own main.go. The utilities are simple\n          enough that any shared abstraction would be premature. Duplication of\n          the read-hash-print loop across four packages is acceptable and preferred\n          over abstraction.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Use only Go standard library packages (crypto/md5, crypto/sha1,\n          crypto/sha256, crypto/sha512, encoding/hex, flag, fmt, io, os) plus\n          pkg/sys for SIGPIPE. Do NOT add any external dependencies.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          For differential tests, use the reference binary names with \"g\" prefix:\n          gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, gsha512sum (Homebrew GNU coreutils).\n          If exec.LookPath fails, call t.Skip. Do NOT attempt to install packages.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"All four binaries compile: go build ./cmd/md5sum ./cmd/sha1sum ./cmd/sha256sum ./cmd/sha512sum\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Each binary produces correct GNU-format output: '<hex-hash>  <filename>' with two-space separator\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Each binary reads from stdin when no file arguments are given\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"The --check flag reads a checksum file and validates each entry, printing OK/FAILED and exiting 1 on mismatch\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/... passes (or skips gracefully if reference binaries are not installed)\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Total production code across all four packages is between 150 and 250 lines\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27516,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27516},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c54928-3f93-4b15-98eb-98ccf3f4621f","uuid":"117298a7-5eb2-4e3b-8477-9a05f501b8e8"}
